Design tokens informed by:

The people and projects below shaped Southpaw's design token
system. We credit them here out of respect for their work.
No source code was copied — these credits acknowledge the
published research, principles, and open-source values that
informed our own implementation.

- Emil Kowalski (@emilkowalski_) — https://emilkowal.ski
  Design Engineer at Linear. Creator of Sonner, Vaul, and
  "Animations on the Web." Southpaw's motion tokens are based
  on his published animation principles and easing curves.
  https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills (MIT)

- Material Design 3 (Google) — https://m3.material.io
  Southpaw's density system uses Material's 4dp decrement
  model and touch target guidelines as a foundation.

- Nathan Curtis (EightShapes) — https://eightshapes.com
  Component sizing and spatial models informed by his articles
  "Size in Design Systems" and "Space in Design Systems."

- Atlassian Design System — https://atlassian.design
  Compact/default density modes and the 8px base unit
  influenced Southpaw's density token scale.
